## [GAP ANALYSIS] Public group members page is silently truncated to 50 with no pager

**Severity:** MEDIUM -- user-visible regression: groups with more than 50 members only show the first 50 on the public members tab.

### The Problem

```js
setupController: function(controller, model) {
  this.controllerFor('group').set('showing', 'members');
  controller.set("model", model);
  model.findMembers();
}
```

`Discourse.Group` now defaults to `limit: 50`, and `GroupsController#members` defaults to `(params[:limit] || 50)`. `discourse/templates/group/members.hbs` just iterates `members`, and it has no next/previous controls. Only the admin template got the pager.

### Theory / Proof

Before this PR, `GroupsController#members` only applied `limit/offset` for `group.automatic?` (default 200). Non-automatic groups returned **all** members. After this PR every group is capped at 50, and the public UI cannot request any later page.

### What happens today vs. what will break

A custom group with 120 members shows 50 names on `/groups/foo/members`. The other 70 cannot be reached from the UI, and nothing tells the user the list is partial.

### Recommendation

Reuse the admin pager on the public page (move `currentPage`/`totalPages`/`next`/`previous` into a shared mixin or onto the model). At minimum, show "showing 50 of N" plus a load-more action:

```hbs
{{#unless showingLast}}<button {{action "next"}} class="btn">{{i18n 'load_more'}}</button>{{/unless}}
```
